<title>UK: TABLE-HSBC H1 pretax profit up 13 pct.</title>
<headline>TABLE-HSBC H1 pretax profit up 13 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>First half to June 30</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		66		     vs up 10 pct</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 20		     vs up 33 pct</p>
<p> Pretax		     2,623		  vs 2,321</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts had forecast pre-tax profits in a range between 2.32 and 2.48 billion stg.</p>
<p>Current H1 charge for bad debts was 158 million stg, which was 19 percent lower than year-ago charge.</p>
<p>In Honk Kong dollar terms, H1 pretax profit was HK$33.18 billion versus HK$27.42 billion.</p>
<p>Full company name - HSBC Holdings Plc. --London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
